    "description": "Link-U Group Inc. engages in the internet service business in Japan. The company develops and operates manga apps. It is also involved in the provision of marketing services; planning, management, and consulting for promotions using Vtubers and streamers; and DX implementation support, promotion, and systems, as well as planning, development, and operation in various fields, including manga apps to government systems. In addition, the company operates Bookhodai, a reading subscription service for individuals and businesses, such as beauty salons and manga cafes; and Yureshiru, an earthquake disaster prevention app. Further, it engages in manga production and distribution for digital manga store; overseas comic distribution services in English, Spanish and other languages; localization and outsourcing distribution of contents; and production and distribution of webtoons based on web novels. The company was formerly known as Link-U Inc. and changed its name to Link-U Group Inc. in February 2024. Link-U Group Inc. was incorporated in 2013 and is headquartered in Chiyoda, Japan."
